  "scope": "Separate test-only RawPoolClient; shipping JavaScript default, Rustls runtime, original SpikeHttpClient constructors and original failed matrices unchanged.",
  "implementation": [
    "Unique HTTP1 sender/driver ownership through actual consumer completion; final-data is_end_stream and header-only handoff do not require an extra poll(None). Drop alone never reports completion or downstream delivery.",
    "Exact Http1Reservation retires before pool return; poisoned/claimed/stale ownership cannot return or claim a later request. Attached and unattached upgrade tokens reject before dialing.",
    "Per-origin LIFO free list with actual256 limit, leading decimal Keep-Alive hint minus1000ms, default5000ms, per-entry generation expiry and actual IO inactivity observations; busy timeout does not close an active request.",
    "Consumer completion resets busy timeout0 before sender readiness; cap check precedes hint policy, accepted insertion alone configures idle timeout. Rejected cap never starts an idle timer. Driver retirement and insertion share the pool lock; callbacks, wake and IO destruction remain outside.",
    "Separate raw/fetch pools, separate origins, actual in-memory synthetic subscription gateway refresh, bounded request/dial cancellation, sibling survival, decoder-error discard, stale-timer rejection, wire Host and path normalization, timer/task/socket cleanup."
  ],
